{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794767198","published":"2026-11-15T18:26:52Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:28:33.831358625Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-116307","CVE-2026-116314","CVE-2026-116316","CVE-2026-116319","CVE-2026-116320","CVE-2026-116326","CVE-2026-116330","CVE-2026-116331","CVE-2026-116332","CVE-2026-116335","CVE-2026-120139","CVE-2026-6460"],"summary":"postgresql: Fix of 13 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-6460: forbid ALTERing a column or composite type used by stored expressions, defaults, constraints or indexes; fix related locking races (partial mitigation: attribute versioning is not backported, so stale composite values held in open cursors, prepared statements or PL/pgSQL variables are not covered)\n- CVE-2026-116307: PL/Perl: refuse to free a prepared query that is being executed\n- CVE-2026-116316: prevent creating types and pg_temp-qualified relations, including CREATE TABLE AS / SELECT INTO targets, in pg_temp from restricted code\n- CVE-2026-116319: PL/Perl: do not save and re-use the temp context in return_next()\n- CVE-2026-116320: PL/Perl: hold a reference on a Perl array or hash while scanning it\n- CVE-2026-116326: PL/Perl: cope with errors thrown from tied or overloaded objects (stale sigjmp_buf)\n- CVE-2026-116330: make \\restrict keys protective in pg_dump --format=tar restore.sql\n- CVE-2026-116331: do not use MinMaxAggPath if the aggregate's input and output types do not match\n- CVE-2026-116332: fix use-after-free due to drop of portals being set up, mark such portals failed during error recovery, ignore not-yet-defined portals in pg_cursors\n- CVE-2026-116335: check that commutator/negator operators return the same data type and reset their links on DROP OPERATOR\n- CVE-2026-120139: protect against int32 overflow in tuple size calculations and harden allocations against integer wraparound\n- CVE-2026-116314: complete the fix (tar header length check, validate file names in the \"files\" archive format)","affected":[{"package":{"nam